"stats.svp.note" = "Each round counts as it was played. “Standardized putting” adds your strokes gained back onto the card: the score the same long game would have shot with tour-average putting.\n\nEach band covers one standard deviation either side of that series' average, and the percentage compares the two.\n\nA narrower standardized band means the putter is what pulls your rounds apart: take it out and they converge. A wider one means the opposite, and it can only happen one way — the putter gained most on the rounds where the rest of the game went worst. That is putting covering for the long game, not putting being irrelevant.\n\nThe average strokes gained is a separate question: it says whether the putter is a net gain or a net cost, not whether it is what makes your rounds differ.";
"stats.svp.bandLegend" = "score average ± spread";
"stats.svp.bandLegendPro" = "standardized putting average ± spread";
"stats.svp.impactHigh" = "PUTTING DRIVES YOUR SCORE";
"stats.svp.impactMedium" = "PUTTING MOVES YOUR SCORE";
"stats.svp.impactLow" = "PUTTING IS NOT THE DIFFERENCE";
