"chart.makeVsTour.info" = "One row per distance bracket: the putts you holed over the putts you took from there, against the tour's average make rate across the same bracket.\n\nThe right-hand column totals PCG for that bracket, divided by the number of rounds.\n\nThe tour column is a flat average across the whole bracket, while PCG measures every putt against the curve at its own distance. So when your putts sit at the near end of a bracket, PCG can come out negative even though your make % is above the tour column.";
"stats.makeBySituation.info" = "The same distance brackets, split by the score each putt was for, so a birdie putt and a par putt from the same range can be compared.\n\nNeeds the score reference (\"putt for\"), which Custom mode can leave out.";
"summary.missTendency.info" = "Every miss placed in the direction it was entered. A sector reddens with how often that direction came up, and the middle holds the total.\n\nNeeds the complex result field: Pro mode, or Custom with the result set to complex — a plain \"missed\" has no direction to place.";
"summary.missReasons.info" = "How often each reason was ticked on a missed putt. A putt with more than one reason is counted once, under \"multiple\".\n\nNeeds the miss reasons field: Pro mode, or Custom with that field added.\n\nUnderneath, every reason is checked against every direction and every kind of putt: break direction and strength, straight, uphill, downhill, the four distance bands, double break. A link is only named when more than 60 percent of a group's misses share the reason, at least 20 points more than the misses it is compared with, and a statistical test backs it. Only rounds where reasons were recorded count.\n\nFor misreads and wrong aims the break is read as well: its direction, its strength (gentle 1 percent, medium 2, strong 3 and more) and the hill. The side of the miss shows whether too little or too much break was played, or on a straight putt which break was seen. For misreads the length shows whether the slope or the pace was misjudged. This is named from 6 such misses, when more than 60 percent went the same way. Underneath each one is the narrowest distance range holding 80 percent of those misses.";
"summary.leaveByMiss.info" = "Average distance left after a miss, grouped by the direction it went — measured from the distance of the next putt on that hole. Bars are scaled to the longest of those averages.\n\nNeeds the complex result field: Pro mode, or Custom with the result set to complex.";

