"game.aroundTheHole.explanation" = "Set five tees at the same distance around the hole: one straight uphill putt to start on, then right-to-left uphill, right-to-left downhill, left-to-right uphill and left-to-right downhill. Hole all five and the lap is done. Miss one and you go back to the first tee — the laps only count unbroken. Shorter putts ask for more laps: five at 1 m, three at 1.3 m, two at 2 m, one at 2.5 m. You can change that, and if you mark the drill as too easy afterwards, the next setup offers a lap more. It is a drill you finish rather than a score you chase, so what it keeps is how long it took and how often you turned up.";
