"game.ladder.goal" = "Trains pace on its own: the ball only has to stop in the right place, so distance control is the whole test.";
"game.ladder.explanation" = "Putt from one spot to a row of target distances, working up the ladder. A putt counts when the ball finishes within 30 cm of its rung — short or long — so nothing has to be holed and the line never comes into it.\n\nTwo ladders to choose from. The large one goes in whole metres from 5 m out to 20 m, which is lag range. The fine one goes in half metres between 5 and 10 m, where the gaps are small enough that the stroke has to be measured rather than felt.\n\nMiss a rung and play it again before moving up. Like the other training drills, the app only asks whether you finished it or gave up — what it keeps is that you turned up and how long it took.";
