"coach.tournament.sameSpread" = "Both sets are equally spread out, so a card counting changes nothing about how reliable you are.";
"coach.tournament.outliers" = "ROUNDS THAT STOOD OUT";
"coach.tournament.outlier" = "%1$@ (%2$@): %3$@ SG — %4$.1f standard deviations from that set's average.";
"coach.tournament.info" = "Your last five tournament rounds against your last five casual ones, reported whichever way it falls — the point is to know what your card says when it counts, and \"no difference\" is an answer to that.\n\nBoth measures are shown so it is clear what is being counted. SG is strokes gained putting over a round: the putts the tour would expect, less the putts you took. PCG is the same round's conversion gain, each putt against the tour's odds of holing it from where it stood.\n\nThe ± underneath is the standard deviation — how far a round typically strays from that average, which is the difference between reliable and merely good on the day. It appears once three rounds stand behind it.\n\nA round is listed as standing out when its SG is at least 1.8 standard deviations from the average of the five it belongs to.";

