"input.missAngle.info" = "Drag around the ring to where the ball stopped, in steps of five degrees: straight short at the bottom, left and right at the sides, up to long-left and long-right at the two ends. The ring is split at the top, so every miss is either left or right.\n\nThe centre is holed and the ring around it a lip-out, as on the board.\n\nOnly the direction is recorded — how far the ball ran is already known from the distance of the next putt.\n\nBelow the sides of the hole counts as short and above them as long, so 85° is still short. The angle reads 0° straight short, 90° beside the hole, and runs back down towards 0° as the miss goes long.";

